# `all[turn & 7][turn & 3]` reads what was stored under numbers on instances of a class: Link proves undefined|null|number|string and unseen objects of it: too wide for a user in the unit to lean on.
# The walk takes no such proof at the read and lays no check there. `get` hands the value on as its result, on whose type its callers lean: the check stands at that door.
# f1 = get
# -- source: a-proof-of-contents-that-says-nothing-is-checked-at-the-door-where-somebody-leans-on-it.js
